.TH MAMA 1 "2026-09-18" "mama 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mama \- your Telugu-speaking terminal buddy
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mama
.RI [ command ]
.br
.B mama
.BR \-\-help | \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mama
prints short, friendly Telugu and Telugu-English messages in your terminal.
Sometimes you need debugging. Sometimes you need motivation. Sometimes you
just need someone to say
.RB \(lq "parledu mama" \(rq
\(em it's alright, mate.
.PP
.RB ( groff
does not render Telugu combining marks, so this page transliterates. The
program itself prints proper Telugu.)
.PP
Run with no arguments,
.B mama
prints a random piece of general wisdom. Each command below draws from its
own collection of messages, selected at random.
.PP
.B mama
is a humour utility. It never executes commands, never modifies your files or
git repositories, and never makes a network request. A message may
.I contain
text such as
.RB \(lq "git commit \-m \[dq]mama said so\[dq]" \(rq,
but that text is only ever printed.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B motivate
Motivation: persistence, discipline, getting back up.
.TP
.B calm
Slow down, breathe, one thing at a time.
.TP
.B morning
A start-of-day nudge.
.TP
.B night
Let the day go and rest.
.TP
.B code
Developer wisdom, mostly with a grin.
.TP
.B git
Git humour.
.TP
.B roast
A playful roast of your code and terminal habits.
.TP
.B coffee
Coffee wisdom.
.TP
.B friday
Weekend mode. Works on any day of the week, deliberately.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
A message was printed.
.TP
.B 1
The command was not recognised, or an unexpected error occurred.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
If set, disable colour entirely. See
.UR https://no-color.org
.UE .
.TP
.B FORCE_COLOR
If set to anything other than
.BR 0 ,
keep colour even when output is not a terminal.
.TP
.B MAMA_SEED
An integer seed for message selection. The same seed always produces the
same message, which is useful in tests and scripts.
.TP
.B MAMA_DEBUG
If set, print real stack traces instead of a friendly apology.
.SH NOTES
.B mama
speaks Telugu, so a UTF-8 locale and a font with Telugu glyphs are required
for readable output. On Debian and Ubuntu, install
.B fonts\-telugu
if you see boxes instead of letters.
.PP
Colour is disabled automatically when standard output is not a terminal, so
.RB \(lq "mama | cat" \(rq
and
.RB \(lq "mama > file" \(rq
produce plain text.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B mama
Print a random piece of wisdom.
.TP
.B mama roast
Print a playful roast.
.TP
.B MAMA_SEED=42 mama motivate
Print the same motivational message every time.
